course: dictionary
lesson: 8455
title: Picturing a new word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A dictionary tells you what a word means, and a clear picture in your head helps you remember it. Read the meaning, then picture the thing. A sailfish is a big ocean fish with a tall fin on its back that looks like a sail.
explain: The meaning gives you clues. A sail is a large cloth that catches the wind on a boat, so the fin looks like one. The long pointed bill is like a sword, so you can spot the fish by its shape.
explain: Now read the sentences. «The sailfish is one of the fastest fish, uses its long thin body and sail to hunt, and changes colour when hunting in groups.» Each clue links back to the meaning: fast, long body, sail, hunting.
explain: Check yourself by swapping the word in. Could you say «The sailfish hunts smaller fish» and have it still make sense? If yes, you understand the word.
fact: A sailfish is a big ocean fish with a tall fin on its back that looks like a sail.
fact: Its long pointed bill is like a sword.
fact: A sailfish is one of the fastest fish in the sea.
fact: A sailfish hunts smaller fish.
exercise: What is a sailfish? | A small pond bird with a long tail | A land animal that runs very fast | A kind of boat with sails | *A big ocean fish with a tall fin like a sail
exercise: «The sailfish uses its long thin body and sail to hunt.» What does a sailfish use its body and sail for? | To hide from the sun | To build a nest | To sing to other fish | *To hunt
exercise: The sailfish has a long pointed bill. What does this bill look like? | Like a sail | *Like a sword | Like a feather | Like a spoon
test: Which fish is one of the fastest in the sea and hunts smaller fish? | *Sailfish | Seahorse | Goldfish | Clownfish
test: In «The sailfish is among the fastest in the water», what does among the fastest mean? | Afraid of the water | The slowest of all | Bigger than all the others | *One of the quickest of all
exam: Which word in the meaning tells you the fin is shaped like something you find on a boat? | ocean | bill | *sail | fish
